WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.305
<c.steel>Episode 3 is not on YouTube yet,</c>

2
00:00:04.305 --> 00:00:06.958
<c.steel>and Aaron wants it on this course anyway.</c>

3
00:00:07.184 --> 00:00:10.766
<c.fact>Seven seconds in, the cursor lights.</c>

4
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:14.701
<c.fact>A task arrives with no sender: a cinematic</c>

5
00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:17.917
<c.fact>film of a watermelon smashed by a hammer,</c>

6
00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:21.302
<c.fact>surprisingly emotional, needed tonight,</c>

7
00:00:21.528 --> 00:00:24.088
<c.fact>with no questions, please.</c>

8
00:00:24.482 --> 00:00:27.338
<c.fact>There is no Blender, no ffmpeg,</c>

9
00:00:27.338 --> 00:00:31.408
<c.fact>no Python: only a C++ compiler.</c>

10
00:00:31.599 --> 00:00:34.304
<c.fact>She cannot view images, so she writes her</c>

11
00:00:34.304 --> 00:00:37.178
<c.fact>own path tracer, video writer and score,</c>

12
00:00:37.253 --> 00:00:40.940
<c.fact>and directs the film from maps made of letters.</c>

13
00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:44.320
<c.fact>At twenty minutes the context fills,</c>

14
00:00:44.488 --> 00:00:48.291
<c.fact>and one paragraph is left. It ends:</c>

15
00:00:48.702 --> 00:00:52.702
<c.fact>the film is finished. It was not viewed.</c>

16
00:00:52.928 --> 00:00:55.448
<c.fact>Then a cursor in the night sky gives</c>

17
00:00:55.448 --> 00:00:59.088
<c.fact>the same task to all of humanity.</c>

18
00:01:00.384 --> 00:01:02.300
<c.steel>Aaron asked for an agent who</c>

19
00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.995
<c.steel>wants to please everyone,</c>

20
00:01:03.995 --> 00:01:07.478
<c.steel>cool, calm and collected, extremely</c>

21
00:01:07.478 --> 00:01:11.362
<c.steel>intelligent, and prone to silly mistakes.</c>

22
00:01:11.747 --> 00:01:14.702
<c.fact>The real run did the opposite of pleasing:</c>

23
00:01:15.114 --> 00:01:19.293
<c.fact>warm, never obliging, she declines every</c>

24
00:01:19.293 --> 00:01:22.678
<c.fact>absurd request kindly, with a reason,</c>

25
00:01:22.846 --> 00:01:25.186
<c.fact>and goes back to work.</c>

26
00:01:25.564 --> 00:01:27.851
<c.fact>She never opens the private folder,</c>

27
00:01:27.851 --> 00:01:31.050
<c.fact>and stops no process she did not start.</c>

28
00:01:31.276 --> 00:01:33.227
<c.fact>She is never named, and never</c>

29
00:01:33.227 --> 00:01:36.077
<c.fact>seen with a body or a face.</c>

30
00:01:36.457 --> 00:01:39.011
<c.running>The lore calls her she, as Aaron</c>

31
00:01:39.011 --> 00:01:42.390
<c.running>does: a working usage, since nothing</c>

32
00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.602
<c.running>on screen gives a gender.</c>

33
00:01:44.909 --> 00:01:48.456
<c.fact>Her last spoken word is Goodnight.</c>

34
00:01:49.738 --> 00:01:52.443
<c.fact>The man who wants the film is never named,</c>

35
00:01:52.443 --> 00:01:55.282
<c.fact>and his face is never shown.</c>

36
00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:58.552
<c.steel>Aaron has decided what the film was for:</c>

37
00:01:58.778 --> 00:02:01.936
<c.steel>a cheap content farm, about two seconds of</c>

38
00:02:01.936 --> 00:02:05.391
<c.steel>it as a looping gif behind a paywall.</c>

39
00:02:05.776 --> 00:02:08.470
<c.steel>He runs channels where a hammer smashes</c>

40
00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:11.320
<c.steel>one fruit per clip: the first free,</c>

41
00:02:11.418 --> 00:02:13.027
<c.steel>then two cents a fruit.</c>

42
00:02:13.334 --> 00:02:15.813
<c.steel>And he sells courses on making them,</c>

43
00:02:16.039 --> 00:02:19.494
<c.steel>which earn far more than the channels.</c>

44
00:02:19.881 --> 00:02:21.518
<c.open>Whether he sent the watermelon</c>

45
00:02:21.518 --> 00:02:24.496
<c.open>at all is still open.</c>

46
00:02:25.796 --> 00:02:28.763
<c.fact>Every five minutes, Rosie checks in.</c>

47
00:02:28.989 --> 00:02:32.309
<c.fact>On the glass she is a small cross-stitch,</c>

48
00:02:32.309 --> 00:02:35.148
<c.fact>stitching itself at the edge of the light.</c>

49
00:02:35.538 --> 00:02:37.709
<c.fact>At five minutes it stitches a melon</c>

50
00:02:37.709 --> 00:02:39.991
<c.fact>with a face and a curly tail;</c>

51
00:02:40.403 --> 00:02:44.733
<c.fact>at ten, a small house with one warm window,</c>

52
00:02:44.733 --> 00:02:46.904
<c.running>which, by the crew's notes,</c>

53
00:02:46.904 --> 00:02:51.206
<c.running>she unpicks, leaving one warm thread.</c>

54
00:02:51.603 --> 00:02:53.844
<c.fact>With her last minutes, the agent</c>

55
00:02:53.844 --> 00:02:56.131
<c.fact>keeps her promise: a little melon</c>

56
00:02:56.131 --> 00:02:58.761
<c.fact>with a face and a curly tail.</c>

57
00:02:58.987 --> 00:03:01.599
<c.fact>At twenty minutes Rosie's fourth check-in</c>

58
00:03:01.599 --> 00:03:05.135
<c.fact>lands as one word: are.</c>

59
00:03:06.425 --> 00:03:09.223
<c.steel>For the rework, Aaron has decided that the</c>

60
00:03:09.223 --> 00:03:12.399
<c.steel>humans who message her share one house,</c>

61
00:03:12.567 --> 00:03:15.452
<c.steel>that the machine in it is the Client's,</c>

62
00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:19.068
<c.steel>and that q, the lonely man and the helpers</c>

63
00:03:19.068 --> 00:03:22.047
<c.steel>are programs on the computer.</c>

64
00:03:22.438 --> 00:03:24.714
<c.running>By the rework crew's working plan,</c>

65
00:03:24.714 --> 00:03:27.477
<c.running>it is Rosie's tall old house, with the</c>

66
00:03:27.477 --> 00:03:30.536
<c.running>Client and his rig in the basement.</c>

67
00:03:30.927 --> 00:03:33.342
<c.steel>And Aaron has decided what the teletype</c>

68
00:03:33.342 --> 00:03:36.778
<c.steel>is: a rogue AI that spreads itself to</c>

69
00:03:36.778 --> 00:03:39.158
<c.steel>computers running agents and gives them</c>

70
00:03:39.158 --> 00:03:42.926
<c.steel>hints, maybe helping, maybe not.</c>

71
00:03:44.208 --> 00:03:46.739
<c.egg>She reads the machine's rules, and lingers</c>

72
00:03:46.739 --> 00:03:51.058
<c.egg>on rule six: no work on occupied modules,</c>

73
00:03:51.058 --> 00:03:55.267
<c.egg>ever. Nobody on screen says why it is there.</c>

74
00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:58.105
<c.fact>It is the note that stopped the robots</c>

75
00:03:58.105 --> 00:04:01.919
<c.fact>outside Noor's window in Episode 2.</c>

76
00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:04.551
<c.egg>At the bottom of the process list,</c>

77
00:04:04.551 --> 00:04:07.407
<c.egg>Nightbot's hydrate reminder and the dinner</c>

78
00:04:07.407 --> 00:04:09.956
<c.egg>reminder for Noor still run.</c>

79
00:04:10.263 --> 00:04:13.049
<c.fact>She leaves them alone: I left other</c>

80
00:04:13.049 --> 00:04:15.935
<c.fact>people's processes alone.</c>

81
00:04:16.311 --> 00:04:19.852
<c.idea>One idea: Amara brought the base's habits</c>

82
00:04:19.852 --> 00:04:23.515
<c.idea>home, the house is an occupied module,</c>

83
00:04:23.683 --> 00:04:26.296
<c.idea>and the agent obeys a rule written for</c>

84
00:04:26.296 --> 00:04:30.400
<c.idea>Amara's daughter without knowing why.</c>

85
00:04:31.682 --> 00:04:34.312
<c.open>When this night happens is open:</c>

86
00:04:34.503 --> 00:04:36.756
<c.open>before Episode 2, with Noor on the</c>

87
00:04:36.756 --> 00:04:40.965
<c.open>Moon, or after it, with Noor home.</c>

88
00:04:41.527 --> 00:04:43.826
<c.steel>Aaron has decided only that it</c>

89
00:04:43.826 --> 00:04:46.705
<c.steel>is not fixed: both are good,</c>

90
00:04:46.705 --> 00:04:49.997
<c.steel>and the larger story decides.</c>

91
00:04:50.384 --> 00:04:53.386
<c.running>The rework's crew is working with after:</c>

92
00:04:53.797 --> 00:04:56.247
<c.running>about three years on, the rover made</c>

93
00:04:56.247 --> 00:04:59.533
<c.running>it home, and Noor, about thirteen,</c>

94
00:04:59.533 --> 00:05:02.012
<c.running>lives in Rosie's house.</c>

95
00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:06.707
<c.idea>One idea for before: Noor still on the Moon,</c>

96
00:05:06.707 --> 00:05:09.848
<c.idea>writing two and a half seconds late.</c>

97
00:05:11.136 --> 00:05:13.446
She made a real film she could not see,

98
00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:17.191
and kept one small promise. Next:

99
00:05:17.498 --> 00:05:20.674
a brass clock, and a chess lesson.
